    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to present No.54 Sandymount Avenue to the market. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a superb property in one of Sandymount’s most sought after residential settings, enjoying an enviable location. Features of the property include private off street parking for four cars, exceptional private grounds, south westerly orientation to the rear garden and a detached residence with distinctive feature porch. Extending to approximately c. 164.9 sq. m the accommodation briefly comprises a entrance hall, living room, dining room, kitchen, three bedrooms and shower room complete the ground floor accommodation. The first floor comprise one bedroom, a study and a family bathroom.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property is approached via a generous, gravelled driveway, providing ample off street parking and surrounded by mature trees, hedging and established planting which create an exceptional sense of privacy and seclusion. The attractive detached residence is enhanced by its distinctive bay window and charming covered porch, adding to its character and appeal.\r\n\r\nTo the rear lies a superb, exceptionally private garden, predominantly laid in lawn and surrounded by an abundance of mature trees, hedging and established planting. The extensive greenery and well established boundaries provide an excellent degree of privacy and seclusion.\r\nThis charming, detached family home presents a rare opportunity to acquire a property of immense character, offering excellent potential to enhance and extend the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\nEntrance Hall: 4.21m  x 6.40m tiled flooring, feature coving, recessed lighting\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 4.48m x 3.93m wood flooring, coving feature bay window to front, original fireplace, built in shelving \r\n\r\nDining Room: 4.59m x 3.93m wood flooring, feature coving, french doors to rear garden \r\n\r\nKitchen: 3.06m x 3.62m tiled flooring, tiled splashback, range of eye to floor level units, induction hob, extractor fan, plumbed for washer/dishwasher, door to the rear garden \r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 4.86m x 4.25m carpet flooring, coving, feature bay window to front \r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 4.20m x 3.30m carpet flooring , feature coving \r\n\r\nBedroom 3: carpet flooring, two windows to front \r\n\r\nShower Room: 2.55m x 2.68m floor to ceiling tiling, recessed lighting, shower unit, w.h.b, w.c.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor \r\nLanding:1.44m x 2.42m \r\n\r\nBedroom 4: 5.11m x 3.61m carpet flooring, recessed lighting \r\n\r\nStudy: 5.11m x3.73m carpet flooring, window to rear, recessed lighting \r\n\r\nBathroom: 1.68m c 2.42m floor to ceiling tiling, bath unit, w.h.b, w.c.\r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area: c. 164.9 sq. m.\r\n\r\nAsking Price: €1,945,000\r\n\r\nBER: F\r\n\r\nBER No.:  117752766\r\n\r\nEnergy Performance Indicator: 54,072  kWh/m2/yr\r\n\r\nSale Negotiator: Marc McGrath"
      },
